["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDataFile", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The from Element treats each to Element as a data file. A data file is an artifact that stores data required or optional for the from Element's functionality. A data file can be a database file, an index file, a log file, an AI model file, a calibration data file, a temporary file, a backup file, and more. For AI training dataset, test dataset, test artifact, configuration data, build input data, and build output data, please consider using the more specific relationship types: trainedOn, testedOn, hasTest, configures, hasInput, and hasOutput, respectively. This relationship does not imply dependency.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/SupportType/deployed", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/SupportType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasMetadata", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Every to Element is metadata about the from Element (from hasMetadata to).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/CreateAction", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "CreationAction represents an event of product creation.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nb35d0a76d3a7434fb817691b2ae55419", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "The level of automation describes a spectrum of system capability, defining\nthe degree of control and decision-making authority a system possesses\nrelative to an external control.\n\nThis classification helps to define the roles and responsibilities of both the\nhuman operator and the automated system. It is a critical component for risk\nassessment, regulatory compliance, and user interface design.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/notAutomated", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "Level 0 - Not automated. No automation. The operator fully controls the system.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Naa8744abbd094c4b93f6a96c169d3d75", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AllDisjointClasses", "globalId", "", ""]
