["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/packageUrl", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A package URL (commonly pronounced and referred to as \"purl\") is an attempt to standardize package representations\nin order to reliably identify and locate software packages.\nA packageUrl is a URL string which represents a package in a\nmostly universal and uniform way across programming languages, package\nmanagers, packaging conventions, tools, APIs and databases.\n\nA packageUrl is composed of seven components:\n\nscheme:type/namespace/name@version?qualifiers#subpath\n\n\nThe definition for each component can be found in the corresponding\nAnnex of this document.\nKnown type definitions can be found in the\nPackage URL type definitions <https://github.com/package-url/purl-spec/blob/b33dda1cf4515efa8eabbbe8e9b140950805f845/PURL-TYPES.rst>.\n\nComponents are designed such that they form a hierarchy from the most\nsignificant on the left to the least significant components on the right.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/AI/standardCompliance", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Standard that an artifact is being complied with.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/ChangeAction", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "ChangeAction", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/SupportType/support", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "The artifact has been released, and is supported from the supplier. There is a validUntilDate that can provide additional information about the duration of support.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/suppliedBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/catalogType", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A catalogType is a mandatory value and shall select one of the existing entries\nin the ExploitCatalogType vocabulary.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N32fb6e9fc82d4e588b0bba4751118b08", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:N7686d6136cd5499a8074dd5992b26122", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SimpleLicensing/customIdToUri", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "**DEPRECATED in SPDX 3.1.**\nUse customIdToLicense instead.\n\nMaps a LicenseRef or AdditionRef string for a Custom License or a Custom\nLicense Addition to its URI ID.\n\n**NOTE:**\nThis property is deprecated and only included for backward compatibility.\nNew documents should use customIdToLicense instead.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
